{"title":"I Like Good Art and I Cannot Lie","link":"https://kottke.org/25/05/i-like-good-art-and-i-cannot-lie","date":1747428283000,"content":"\n        <p>I was reminded the other day of what a curated treasure trove of art <a href=\"https://20x200.com\">20x200</a> is. So I took a spin through their archive and pulled out some favorites. First up are <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/kennedy-prints/products/kennedy-prints-always-choose-happy\">these Always Choose Happy prints</a> from <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/kennedyprints/\">Amos Kennedy</a> (I also like his <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/kennedy-prints/products/i-support-public-libraries\">Book Lovers Never Go to Bed Alone prints</a>):</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-01.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-01.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-01.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"1000\" alt=\"a stack of colorful prints that say 'Always Choose Happy'\" /></p>\n\n<p>I don’t think I’ve ever seen <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/new-releases-2023/products/carleton-watkins-solar-eclipse\">this solar eclipse photo from Carleton Watkins</a> before. Wow:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-02.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-02.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-02.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"769\" alt=\"photo of a solar eclipse over a bank of clouds\" /></p>\n\n<blockquote><p>Taken on July 29, 1878, Solar Eclipse by canonized landscape photographer Carleton Watkins powerfully, elegantly captures the exact moment the moon completely blocked the sun and cast a surreal shadow over the Earth. Watkins, known for his pioneering work depicting the American West, used this rare event as an opportunity to simultaneously experiment with photographic techniques and record a celestial occurrence. The piece’s resulting artistic and technical achievement is as sublime and awe-inspiring as the eclipse itself. It’s stunning that then, as now, eclipses humble us all by reminding us of our smallness in a vast and fascinatingly ordered universe.</p></blockquote>\n\n<p>Sergei Prokudin-Gorskii was a pioneer in color photography; he documented his native Russia in color from 1904 to 1915. <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/sergei-prokudin-gorskii/products/sergei-prokudin-gorskii-siren\">Here’s his photograph of some flowers</a> (lilacs? hydrangeas?):</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-03.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-03.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-03.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"988\" alt=\"vivid color photo of a bush with pink flowers\" /></p>\n\n<p>We all might need some <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/new-releases-2023/products/jenn-graves-rest\">Rest</a> right now:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-04.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-04.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-04.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"1000\" alt=\"a print that says 'REST' in several overlapping colors\" /></p>\n\n<p>I love <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/gordon-parks\">the photographic work of Gordon Parks</a>; this one is called <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/gordon-parks/products/gordon-parks-camp-fern-rock-archer\">Camp Fern Rock (archer)</a>:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-05.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-05.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-05.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"991\" alt=\"black and white photo of a woman shooting a bow\" /></p>\n\n<p>If you’ve lived in NYC for any length of time, you can’t help but be a little bit curious and charmed by the now-abandoned <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/new-releases-2023/products/detroit-photographic-company-city-hall-subway-station-new-york\">City Hall subway station</a>:</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-06.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-06.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/20x200-06.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"798\" alt=\"black and white photo of a subway station with a curving track\" /></p>\n\n<p>They also have a bunch of stuff from <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/jason-polan\">Jason Polan</a>, <a href=\"https://kottke.org/20/02/an-international-eye-test-chart-circa-1907\">this amazing eye test chart</a>, <a href=\"https://20x200.com/collections/hilma-af-klint\">prints of several works by Hilma af Klint</a>, and the <a href=\"https://kottke.org/19/06/the-marvelous-mississippi-river-meander-maps\">The Marvelous Mississippi River Meander Maps</a>.</p>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/20x200\">20x200</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/art\">art</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/photography\">photography</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/05/i-like-good-art-and-i-cannot-lie\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"f888edf98b040d9e1d883e8b7737fb268953f496c98281d761b12f4651bf05c7","category":"Sites"}